        <mxCell id="c154" value="The month of the first surge day" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="390" y="422" width="250" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c155" value="&lt;i&gt;93 surge days in all, none before &lt;span style=&quot;white-space:nowrap&quot;&gt;2024-05-31&lt;/span&gt;. A surge day is a manufacturing day on which every employee who clocked in recorded the same hours (test H8). The most in a month rose from 3 in 2024 to 7 in October 2026, and the share of the year&#x27;s manufacturing overtime that falls on surge days rose from 35.5% to 70.5%. A month with no bar had no surge day. The time records end on &lt;span style=&quot;white-space:nowrap&quot;&gt;2026-12-11&lt;/span&gt;, so the last month is partial.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="450" width="860" height="57" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
